data: {"type": "result", "answer": {"response": "This counts how many tracks belong to each media type. It joins the media types list with the tracks table on the media type identifier, counts the tracks per media type, includes any media type with no tracks as zero, and groups the results by media type name.", "sql_code": "SELECT mt.\"Name\" AS MediaTypeName, COUNT(t.\"TrackId\") AS TrackCount FROM \"MediaType\" AS mt LEFT JOIN \"Track\" AS t ON mt.\"MediaTypeId\" = t.\"MediaTypeId\" GROUP BY mt.\"MediaTypeId\", mt.\"Name\" ORDER BY mt.\"Name\"", "sql_columns": ["65fda549-19fd-4d9e-a718-df82c38b36f2", "55050c6c-01f3-4b2b-b892-cb41f38c374f", "edccac4a-f991-4d60-ac6b-c566c06c5acb", "2d18794a-b916-49a8-8faf-8839a3fee548"], "custom_analyses_used": [], "sql_response_from_db": ["[{\"MediaTypeName\":\"AAC audio file\",\"TrackCount\":11},{\"MediaTypeName\":\"MPEG audio file\",\"TrackCount\":3034},{\"MediaTypeName\":\"Protected AAC audio file\",\"TrackCount\":237},{\"MediaTypeName\":\"Protected MPEG-4 video file\",\"TrackCount\":214},{\"MediaTypeName\":\"Purchased AAC audio file\",\"TrackCount\":7}]"], "thoughts": "- Preparing candidates: The question asks about the count of tracks per media type, so the primary grouping/focus is on the media type column.\n- Preparing candidates: The question asks for the count of tracks per media type. MediaType provides the grouping/labeling (Name) and Track provides the tracks to count (joined via MediaTypeId). PlaylistTrack and InvoiceLine are unrelated to grouping tracks by media type and would only change row counts if joined.\n- Constructing SQL: The question asks for the count of tracks per media type. I'll join MediaType to Track on MediaTypeId and group by media type name. I'll use a LEFT JOIN so media types with zero tracks are included with a count of 0, because the question says \"each media type\" which implies all media types should appear. I'll count TrackId (non-nullable) so zero-row media types yield 0. No time window, ties, or division concerns apply.\n- Validating SQL and intent: The query joins MediaType to Track on MediaTypeId (the verified path), groups by media type, and counts TrackId per media type\u2014correctly answering how many tracks each media type has."}}

